CC0 1.0 Universal — Public Domain Dedication

The person who associated a work with this deed has dedicated the work to the
public domain by waiving all of his or her rights to the work worldwide under
copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights, to the extent
allowed by law.

You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial
purposes, all without asking permission.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

WHY CC0 AND NOT A MORE PROTECTIVE LICENCE

A shared vocabulary is worth something only if anyone can adopt it without
asking, without attribution obligations, and without checking whether their
licence is compatible with someone else's. Attribution is welcome and the
sources are all named in CLAIMS.md, but requiring it would put friction in
exactly the place this proposal needs none.
